@startuml
title Deployment -- three roles, one reason

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "godecane / godestorm (local)" {
  folder "maven-tools" {
    [jqa-nightly] as N
    database "store-work" as W
    database "publish/blue" as B
    database "publish/green" as G
    database "scratch/data" as S
  }
  node "Docker" {
    [jqa-neo4j-published\nbolt 7688 -- READ ONLY] as PUB
    [jqa-neo4j-scratch\nbolt 7689 -- writable] as SCR
  }
  [MCP server\njqassistant] as MCP
}

node "aschemann.net (planned)" {
  [Neo4j\ndefault_to_read_only=true] as REMOTE
  database "blue | green" as RSLOT
}

N --> W : writes offline
W --> B : jqa-publish (rsync + verify + switch)
W --> G
B --> PUB : current symlink
G --> PUB
S --> SCR
MCP --> SCR : ad-hoc, writable

B ..> RSLOT : rsync delta\n(~7% of the store)
RSLOT --> REMOTE

note bottom of REMOTE
  Neo4j Community has no roles and no runtime
  ACCESS switch, so an instance is either writable
  for everyone or read-only for everyone. The public
  one therefore has no write path at all -- and needs
  no credentials, in particular no GitHub token.
end note
@enduml
